l Engine 5.8\n\nThe user attempted multiple connection methods but all resulted in immediate disconnection, suggesting a systemic issue rather than client-specific configuration problems.","durationMs":4204,"url":"https://forums.unrealengine.com/t/5-8-experimental-modelcontextprotocol-mcp-server-instantly-drops-connections/2729488"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d6bf4200-fd88-46bd-9a2c-57f9cebf0b92","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","sessionId":"e3b338da-ab86-4243-90e2-fe8410b66d35","version":"2.1.221","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"e2a05bd5-ce3c-49a0-a6ea-8a718b2873d4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e16bb861-c3ed-444c-954b-fa9801706d55","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QCDNPXBBNHDLRtU65qo2zE","type":"tool_result","content":"# Unreal MCP Setup Guide\n\n## Plugin Installation\n1. Open **Edit > Plugins**\n2. Search for and enable **Unreal MCP**\n3. Search for and enable **All Toolsets**\n4. The **Toolset Registry** plugin enables automatically as a dependency\n5. Restart the editor when prompted\n\n## Configuration\nNavigate to **Edit > Editor Preferences > General > Model Context Protocol** to access these settings:\n\n- **Auto Start Server**: Toggle to automatically launch the MCP server on editor startup\n- **Server Port Number**: Default is `8000`\n- **Server URL Path**: Default is `/mcp`\n\nWhen disabled, start the server manually via console command.\n\n## Console Commands\n\nExecute these from the editor console (backtick key by default):\n\n```\nModelContextProtocol.StartServer\nModelContextProtocol.GenerateClientConfig ClaudeCode\nModelContextProtocol.RefreshTools\nModelContextProtocol.StopServer\n```\n\nThe `GenerateClientConfig` command creates a `.mcp.json` file in your project root. Supported client names include ClaudeCode, Cursor, VSCode, Gemini, Codex, and All.\n\n## Connecting Claude Code\n\n1. Generate the config: `ModelContextProtocol.GenerateClientConfig ClaudeCode`\n2. Launch Claude Code from your project root directory\n3. Claude Code automatically discovers the `.mcp.json` configuration\n4. The server binds to `http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp`\n\n## Key Limitations\n\n- \"Supports HTTP and Server-Sent Events only. The `stdio` and WebSocket transports are not supported.\"\n- Loopback connections only; no remote access by default\n- No authentication layer implemented\n- Live Coding doesn't support adding new `UFUNCTION` declarations without a full restart"}]},"uuid":"8883379c-4bf1-4e34-b3b9-4b1d56a28ef9","timestamp":"2026-08-07T09:26:31.552Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":226510,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Unreal MCP Setup Guide\n\n## Plugin Installation\n1. Open **Edit > Plugins**\n2. Search for and enable **Unreal MCP**\n3. Search for and enable **All Toolsets**\n4. The **Toolset Registry** plugin enables automatically as a dependency\n5. Restart the editor when prompted\n\n## Configuration\nNavigate to **Edit > Editor Preferences > General > Model Context Protocol** to access these settings:\n\n- **Auto Start Server**: Toggle to automatically launch the MCP server on editor startup\n- **Server Port Number**: Default is `8000`\n- **Server URL Path**: Default is `/mcp`\n\nWhen disabled, start the server manually via console command.\n\n## Console Commands\n\nExecute these from the editor console (backtick key by default):\n\n```\nModelContextProtocol.StartServer\nModelContextProtocol.GenerateClientConfig ClaudeCode\nModelContextProtocol.RefreshTools\nModelContextProtocol.StopServer\n```\n\nThe `GenerateClientConfig` command creates a `.mcp.json` file in your project root. Supported client names include ClaudeCode, Cursor, VSCode, Gemini, Codex, and All.\n\n## Connecting Claude Code\n\n1. Generate the config: `ModelContextProtocol.GenerateClientConfig ClaudeCode`\n2. Launch Claude Code from your project root directory\n3. Claude Code automatically discovers the `.mcp.json` configuration\n4. The server binds to `http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp`\n\n## Key Limitations\n\n- \"Supports HTTP and Server-Sent Events only. The `stdio` and WebSocket transports are not supported.\"\n- Loopback connections only; no remote access by default\n- No authentication layer implemented\n- Live Coding doesn't support adding new `UFUNCTION` declarations without a full restart","durationMs":7607,"url":"https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/unreal-engine/unreal-mcp-in-unreal-editor?lang=en-US"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e2a05bd5-ce3c-49a0-a6ea-8a718b2873d4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","sessionId":"e3b338da-ab86-4243-90e2-fe8410b66d35","version":"2.1.221","gitBranch":"main"}
